# runtime, not source: what the local admin panel writes and what the upload
# leaves behind. The archive itself was never here — it lives on the drive.
__pycache__/
added/
deleted/
photos/
data/upload.log
data/upload_list.txt
deploy/.shira-media.rendered

# intermediate build products — rebuilt from the drive by scripts/*.py
data/raw_inventory.json
data/durations.json
data/hash_cache.json
data/duplicates.json
data/recordings.json
data/tracks.json

# The editor's own work is NOT ignored, and must not be.
#
# additions, overrides, performers and removed were once filed here as "local
# admin state", and that was wrong: they are not state, they are the editing
# itself — the corrected titles, the descriptions, the singers' names, the
# recordings taken down. The web edition builds its catalogue out of exactly
# these four files beside catalog.json, so anything not committed here simply
# does not exist online.
#
# It cost us: overrides.json sat at 39 entries on this machine and {} on the
# live site, and a singer named there — שלום ששוני — showed up online as
# "לא ידוע". Nothing reported it, because an ignored file never appears in
# git status and so never appears in a "what is left to push" check either.
#
# They are tracked now. scripts/publish_check.py compares them against what
# the live site is actually serving.
data/purge_log.json
